"build:instruction-tuning-sft":{"site":"build","slug":"instruction-tuning-sft","title":"Instruction tuning: from text to answers","url":"https://build.amaete.com/instruction-tuning-sft/","blurb":"A farmers' cooperative in Iowa turns a base model, which only continues text, into an assistant that answers.","checks":[{"q":"What does SFT mainly teach?","a":["A behaviour: responding to instructions","New facts","A new tokenizer"],"ok":0,"why":"The knowledge is already there."},{"q":"Why mask the loss to assistant tokens?","a":["So it learns to answer, not to write user turns","To save memory","To speed up training"],"ok":0,"why":"User tokens give context only."},{"q":"What causes catastrophic forgetting in SFT?","a":["A learning rate far too high","Too few epochs","The loss mask"],"ok":0,"why":"Use about 2e-5, not 3e-4."}]},
